    {
      "id": "2b1919f4-a330-4773-9077-e9df495e60dd",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3600,
        176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1056,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Workflow Overview: Automated Churn Classification & Reporting\n\nThis workflow acts as an automated **Churn Classification Engine** for your SaaS metrics. It captures subscription cancellations, performs a historical check against payment failure (dunning) records in Google Sheets, and mathematically classifies the churn type based on recent billing events. By automating the categorization of involuntary versus voluntary churn and deploying an AI agent to generate monthly executive summaries, it ensures leadership has immediate visibility into solvable revenue leaks versus product-related attrition.\n\n## How it works\n\nThis workflow acts as an automated **Revenue Insights System** for your business. It automatically monitors for subscription cancellations, standardizes the customer data, and cross-references your database for active payment failures.\nIf a payment failure occurred within the allowed window prior to cancellation, the system classifies the revenue loss as involuntary and logs the result. At the end of every month, a scheduled branch dynamically aggregates the classified data, feeds the metrics to an AI engine to draft a concise analytical summary, and instantly emails the formatted HTML performance report to your team.\n\n## Setup Steps\n\n**Trigger: Cancellation Event** \u2014 Start the workflow when a subscription cancellation is detected.\n**Format Cancellation Data** \u2014 Standardize the incoming payload to isolate the customer ID, revenue, and date.\n**Fetch Dunning History** \u2014 Query Google Sheets for any recent, unresolved payment failure records matching the customer.\n**Validate Dunning Window** \u2014 Execute mathematical logic to verify the payment failed before cancellation.\n**Is Involuntary Churn?** \u2014 Route the workflow based on the presence of a valid payment failure sequence.\n**Assign Churn Category** \u2014 Classify the event definitively as Involuntary or Voluntary with contextual notes.\n**Log Churn Event** \u2014 Append the structured classification result into the master tracking database.\n**Trigger: Monthly Rollup** \u2014 Initiate the reporting pipeline automatically on a fixed monthly schedule.\n**Fetch Churn Log** \u2014 Retrieve the historical classification records for the previous billing cycle.\n**Calculate Monthly Metrics** \u2014 Dynamically sum the counts and revenue lost grouped by churn category.\n**Generate AI Narrative** \u2014 Feed the aggregated metrics into Gemini to draft a structured executive summary.\n**Enforce JSON Schema** \u2014 Ensure the AI output strictly adheres to the required title and summary format.\n**Email Executive Report** \u2014 Deliver the finalized, formatted HTML insights directly to your team's inbox."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
